{"id": "g2_min_rooms_closed_bookings", "signature": "solve(bookings)", "statement": "`bookings` is a list of [start, end] pairs of integers describing CLOSED intervals [start, end], meaning both endpoints are included. Two bookings conflict when they share at least one point, so [1, 3] and [3, 5] conflict. A pair with start > end is invalid and is ignored; start == end is a valid single-point booking. Return the minimum number of rooms needed so that no two conflicting bookings share a room. Return 0 for an empty list or when every pair is invalid.", "tests": [{"args": [[]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[[1, 3], [3, 5]]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[[1, 2], [3, 4]]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[[1, 5], [2, 6], [3, 7]]], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[[4, 4], [4, 4]]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[[5, 1]]], "expected": 0}, {"args": [[[0, 10], [10, 20], [20, 30]]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4]]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[[1, 10], [2, 3], [4, 5], [6, 7]]], "expected": 2}, {"args": [[[-5, -1], [-3, 0], [-2, -2]]], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[[7, 9], [1, 3], [4, 6]]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[[1, 4], [2, 6], [5, 8], [3, 3]]], "expected": 3}, {"args": [[[0, 0], [1, 1]]], "expected": 1}, {"args": [[[2, 8], [5, 5], [5, 5], [9, 4]]], "expected": 3}], "facts": [["arg", "bookings", "interval_list"], ["iterate", "bookings"], ["ask", "max_overlap"], ["interval_ends", "closed"], ["size", "bookings", "tiny"]], "deps": {"schema": ["interval_scan"], "uses": ["interval_max_overlap"], "solution_sha256": "77e35777f402392a49afd7ba58cd8fb829fab90e4fd9b7730ba3936e6987385e", "reference_sha256": "c1a4144d0bb44f3b2d2ff3d17cc185ecab5ce27bd5cac95247453e8f2d709ccf"}}